# Backup credentials (deploy/backup.env, mode 600, NOT sourced by the app).
# Keeping RESTIC_* / AWS_* out of .env means a web-app RCE cannot read the
# credential that deletes or encrypts the offsite repository.
# Quoting: RESTIC_PASSWORD and AWS_* below are forwarded from the script's
# environment (`-e VAR`), so normal quoting is fine. Any ADDITIONAL restic/AWS
# variable (e.g. RESTIC_CACHE_DIR, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION) reaches the container via
# `docker --env-file`, which does NOT strip quotes — leave those unquoted.
# Non-secret names the script also needs (same values as .env):
POSTGRES_USER=""
POSTGRES_DB=""
# M6 P2: needed by the Backrest hook, which runs pg_dump INSIDE the backrest
# container (BACKUP_PG_MODE=local) — the container has no Docker socket on
# purpose. Keep this identical to POSTGRES_PASSWORD in .env: a rotation has to
# touch both files (`deploy/compose-prod.sh up` refuses an empty value here).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=""
DATA_DIR=""
# Where backup.sh stages pg.dump. The backrest service bind-mounts the SAME path
# (as /staging) using the BACKUP_DIR of .env, so the dump the schedule validates
# is the one a manual restore picks up. Keep both in sync.
BACKUP_DIR=""
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=""
RESTIC_PASSWORD=""
# Config backup (T3-A): a SECOND repository with a DIFFERENT password. .env is
# never written to the data repository, so a leaked data repository and its
# password cannot decrypt BETTER_AUTH_SECRET / SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY / the DB
# password. Use a separate bucket (preferred) or a `/config` prefix; keep this
# password offline next to RESTIC_PASSWORD.
RESTIC_CONFIG_REPOSITORY=""
RESTIC_CONFIG_PASSWORD=""
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
# Dedicated healthchecks.io check; pinged only on a successful backup.
BACKUP_PING_URL=""
# A success ping also requires the staging dump to be younger than this (minutes),
# so a cancel that leaves yesterday's dump behind cannot look like a good night.
# Optional; the hook defaults to 1440 (24h — a first full upload can take hours;
# the per-run marker is the precise signal, this is only the stale-marker ceiling).
BACKUP_PING_MAX_AGE_MIN=""
# Separate check for the CONFIG repository (the .env with BETTER_AUTH_SECRET /
# SUPPRESSION_HMAC_KEY / the db password). One URL for both repositories would
# let a green data run mask a red config run, so it is deliberately a second
# check; unset ⇒ the config plan only logs.
CONFIG_PING_URL=""
# Separate weekly check (restic check) — silence here means integrity checks stopped.
CHECK_PING_URL=""
# Same, for the config repository's own check. Unset ⇒ log only.
CHECK_PING_URL_CONFIG=""
#
# Optional, rarely touched:
#   BACKUP_LOCK_STALE_MIN  minutes before a .pg-dump.lock left by a crashed run is
#                          considered stale and removed (default 360). Both
#                          producers — the Backrest hook and a manual run — take
#                          that lock, so a stuck lock looks like "another backup
#                          is already writing".
#   BACKUP_RUN_MARKER      container path of the per-run marker the start hook
#                          writes and the end hook compares the dump against
#                          (default /tmp/web-lair-backup-run-start). Container
#                          only: change it in both hooks together, not here.
#
# NOT here: the Backrest schedule knobs (BACKREST_DATA_CRON, *_CHECK_CRON,
# *_PRUNE_CRON, BACKREST_INSTANCE, BACKREST_RENDER_CONFIG). Those are compose
# variables in compose.prod.yaml, so they are read from `.env` / the shell — a
# value in this file would not reach the interpolation.
